{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 3873464,
  "courseSlug": "nextjs-react-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25145786",
      "title": "Using the \"useSWR\" NextJS Hook",
      "lectureOrder": 289,
      "videoOrder": 269,
      "sourceHash": "ac33b4c0f610b1ac51f53179cc9f867990ae121d2dfed776184078280e1a8bac",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 4.05,
          "en": "Now, you can absolutely write",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.05,
          "end": 7.23,
          "en": "this client side data fetching code on your own,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.23,
          "end": 10.33,
          "en": "as we did it here, there's nothing wrong with that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.33,
          "end": 12.33,
          "en": "And you might have good reasons to do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.33,
          "end": 15.34,
          "en": "because this, of course, gives you full control",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.34,
          "end": 17.26,
          "en": "over the entire component state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.26,
          "end": 20.38,
          "en": "and how exactly data is being fetched.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.38,
          "end": 23.32,
          "en": "But this is also such a common pattern",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.32,
          "end": 27.04,
          "en": "that you could consider creating your own custom hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.04,
          "end": 29.16,
          "en": "to outsource this logic into it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.16,
          "end": 33.42,
          "en": "or to use a third-party hook created by someone else.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.42,
          "end": 37.32,
          "en": "And you can look into the SWR hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.32,
          "end": 42.32,
          "en": "If you Google for use SWR you will find swr.vercel.app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.86,
          "end": 47.95,
          "en": "This is a React hook developed by the Next.js team,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.95,
          "end": 52.25,
          "en": "but you can use it in non-Next.js projects as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 52.25,
          "end": 53.77,
          "en": "In the end, this is a hook which,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.77,
          "end": 57.6,
          "en": "under the hood, still will send a HTTP request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 57.6,
          "end": 61.73,
          "en": "by default using the fetch API, which we also used,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 61.73,
          "end": 64.62,
          "en": "but it gives you a couple of nice built in features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.62,
          "end": 69.62,
          "en": "like caching and automatic revalidation retries on error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 70.97,
          "end": 74.64,
          "en": "And you don't have to write all that code on your own.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 74.64,
          "end": 78.08,
          "en": "Instead, you can use this hook in a much simpler way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 78.08,
          "end": 81.46000000000001,
          "en": "The strange name SWR, by the way, stands",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 81.46000000000001,
          "end": 85.35,
          "en": "for stale-while-revalidate, which is the name of this hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 85.35,
          "end": 90.06,
          "en": "because this hook has a built in features for caching data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 90.06,
          "end": 94.31,
          "en": "and revalidating data to give you the most up-to-date data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 94.31,
          "end": 98.74000000000001,
          "en": "without you noticing in a positive way, and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 98.74000000000001,
          "end": 100.24000000000001,
          "en": "Now, you can dive into the docs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 100.24000000000001,
          "end": 102.35,
          "en": "of this hook to learn all about it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 102.35,
          "end": 105.21000000000001,
          "en": "because you can definitely also create",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 105.21000000000001,
          "end": 107.32,
          "en": "a short course about this hook here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 107.32,
          "end": 111.49000000000001,
          "en": "but getting started with it, thankfully, is super simple.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 111.49000000000001,
          "end": 114.99000000000001,
          "en": "In our project, we just need to quit the dev server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 114.99000000000001,
          "end": 117.4,
          "en": "and install it as a package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 117.4,
          "end": 120.65,
          "en": "With npm install swr we install",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 120.65,
          "end": 124.393,
          "en": "this SWR hook package into our project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 125.54,
          "end": 129.4,
          "en": "Now, in last sales, if you want to use it, we can import it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 129.4,
          "end": 134.4,
          "en": "We can import useSWR from 'swr' just like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 136.47,
          "end": 139.843,
          "en": "This imports the hook, it's the same example you see here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 140.71,
          "end": 144.18,
          "en": "And now you can use this hook in your component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 144.18,
          "end": 145.99,
          "en": "so not inside of useEffect,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 145.99,
          "end": 147.98,
          "en": "but directly in your component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 147.98,
          "end": 150.77,
          "en": "all React hooks must be used directly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 150.77,
          "end": 153.88,
          "en": "in a component, not in some nested function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 153.88,
          "end": 156.143,
          "en": "And we use it by simply executing it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 157.44,
          "end": 160.14,
          "en": "Now, this hook wants at least one argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 160.14,
          "end": 163.95,
          "en": "which is an identifier for the request it should send,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 163.95,
          "end": 167.53,
          "en": "typically, the URL of that request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 167.53,
          "end": 170.36,
          "en": "And it's also called an identifier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 170.36,
          "end": 173.54,
          "en": "because this hook will bundle multiple requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 173.54,
          "end": 177.47,
          "en": "to the same URL, which are sent in a certain timeframe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 177.47,
          "end": 182.47,
          "en": "into one request to avoid sending dozens of small requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 182.83,
          "end": 187.23,
          "en": "Not an issue we'll have here, but nice to have in general.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 187.23,
          "end": 190.68,
          "en": "So, we can grab our URL here as an identifier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 190.68,
          "end": 192.86,
          "en": "because it will then conveniently use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 192.86,
          "end": 195.913,
          "en": "this identifier as a URL as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 196.98,
          "end": 200.603,
          "en": "And in the simplest form, this is all we have to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 201.51,
          "end": 205.75,
          "en": "You can add a second argument, which is a fetcher function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 205.75,
          "end": 207.67000000000002,
          "en": "which is a function that describes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 207.67000000000002,
          "end": 209.85,
          "en": "how the request should be sent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 209.85,
          "end": 213.16,
          "en": "But the default is that it will use the fetch API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 213.16,
          "end": 216.63,
          "en": "So, if we want to stick to that default, which I do here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 216.63,
          "end": 219,
          "en": "we don't need to change anything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 219,
          "end": 222.45,
          "en": "Instead, we just call useSWR, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 222.45,
          "end": 225.76,
          "en": "And the request to this URL will be sent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 225.76,
          "end": 228.17000000000002,
          "en": "when this component is loaded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 228.17000000000002,
          "end": 230.05,
          "en": "So, now, we can work with the data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 230.05,
          "end": 232.18,
          "en": "which is returned by that hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 232.18,
          "end": 234.44,
          "en": "And that will be an object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 234.44,
          "end": 237.28,
          "en": "which we can destructure therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 237.28,
          "end": 241.42,
          "en": "which contains the data that was fetched eventually,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 241.42,
          "end": 244.32,
          "en": "and potential error information.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 244.32,
          "end": 248.14,
          "en": "So, I'll use the exact same object destructuring here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 248.14,
          "end": 251.12,
          "en": "and pull out the data, which we eventually get,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 251.12,
          "end": 253.183,
          "en": "and the error, which we might get.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 254.05,
          "end": 257.64,
          "en": "Down here, in our custom code, we have no error handling,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 257.64,
          "end": 259.74,
          "en": "but now we can easily implement it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 259.74,
          "end": 262.09,
          "en": "by just using this extra piece of data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 262.09,
          "end": 264.703,
          "en": "which we get by the useSWR hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 265.95,
          "end": 269.44,
          "en": "So now, with that, we can comment out our custom hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 269.44,
          "end": 271.18,
          "en": "We could also delete it but I want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 271.18,
          "end": 273.45,
          "en": "to keep it around for a reference.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 273.45,
          "end": 277.03,
          "en": "We can also comment out our custom states though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 277.03,
          "end": 280.26,
          "en": "And, now, we can work with data and error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 280.26,
          "end": 284.63,
          "en": "If we don't have data yet, then we know that we're loading.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 284.63,
          "end": 288.02,
          "en": "So, here I'll check if not data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 288.02,
          "end": 291,
          "en": "if we don't have data yet, then I return Loading...",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 291.90999999999997,
          "end": 294.34000000000003,
          "en": "If we have an error, on the other hand,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 294.34000000000003,
          "end": 297.57,
          "en": "I wanna show an error message here, like Failed to load",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 298.92,
          "end": 303.23,
          "en": "and we should move that in front of the, if data check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 303.23,
          "end": 306.48,
          "en": "because an error is more important than the loading state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 306.48,
          "end": 308.503,
          "en": "If we have an error, I wanna show it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 310.05,
          "end": 313.66,
          "en": "Now, if we don't have an error and we do have data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 313.66,
          "end": 316.49,
          "en": "so if we make it past these two if checks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 316.49,
          "end": 318.923,
          "en": "then we can output the data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 320.28,
          "end": 322.58,
          "en": "Now, the problem we'll then face, however,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 322.58,
          "end": 325.46,
          "en": "is that, as I mentioned, the data we get back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 325.46,
          "end": 328.54,
          "en": "from Firebase is not in the right format.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 328.54,
          "end": 330.55,
          "en": "We need to transform it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 330.55,
          "end": 334.29,
          "en": "Now, to work around that issue we got two main approaches.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 334.29,
          "end": 337.04,
          "en": "We could define our own fetcher function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 337.04,
          "end": 340.76,
          "en": "you can learn about that here in the SWR docs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 340.76,
          "end": 342.53,
          "en": "to basically fine tune",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 342.53,
          "end": 345.83,
          "en": "how exactly data will be fetched and returned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 345.83,
          "end": 348.37,
          "en": "Or we, again, use useEffect but,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 348.37,
          "end": 350.3,
          "en": "now, not for sending the request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 350.3,
          "end": 353.17,
          "en": "but for simply transforming the data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 353.17,
          "end": 357.43,
          "en": "So then, here, our dependency would be the data which we get",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 357.43,
          "end": 360.76,
          "en": "because I want to rerun this whenever we got new data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 360.76,
          "end": 362.41,
          "en": "And in useEffect, I want to check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 362.41,
          "end": 365.35,
          "en": "if we do have data, because if we don't have data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 365.35,
          "end": 367.28,
          "en": "there is nothing we need to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 367.28,
          "end": 370.24,
          "en": "But if I do have data, then I wanna go",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 370.24,
          "end": 372.97,
          "en": "through these transformation steps here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 372.97,
          "end": 375.433,
          "en": "So, I'll copy this code from down there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 376.46,
          "end": 381.46,
          "en": "comment this in, and then bring back my sales state here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 381.68,
          "end": 383.88,
          "en": "so that I can set this state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 383.88,
          "end": 387.41,
          "en": "after we transformed the data here in useEffect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 387.41,
          "end": 390.45,
          "en": "So here, instead of this if check still,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 390.45,
          "end": 393.42,
          "en": "instead of useEffect, I'll then set my sales",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 393.42,
          "end": 397.40999999999997,
          "en": "to the transform sales, which are now based",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 397.40999999999997,
          "end": 401.547,
          "en": "on the data, the data key we're getting from useSWR.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 403.14,
          "end": 405.75,
          "en": "So, now, we have our own transformation logic here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 405.75,
          "end": 408.963,
          "en": "which will be kicked off as soon as data was fetched.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 410.07,
          "end": 412.21,
          "en": "And that means that now, again, down there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 412.21,
          "end": 415.07,
          "en": "we can check that even if we have data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 415.07,
          "end": 417.54,
          "en": "it might not have been transformed yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 417.54,
          "end": 419.26,
          "en": "So, if we don't have sales yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 419.26,
          "end": 421.1,
          "en": "which is our transformed data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 421.1,
          "end": 424.25,
          "en": "I still return a paragraph where I also say Loading...,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 424.25,
          "end": 426.63,
